__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Never commit an Asana state dump: task notes carry competitor strategy,
# pricing governance, legal boundaries and the threat model, and this repo is
# PUBLIC. One was pushed on 2026-08-06 and had to be removed.
reports/asana-backup-*.json

# Rescued body text from SEARCHFIRST_WWW_v1 before it was deleted (2026-08-07).
# 325 records, 6MB, the only copy of those bodies. Chapter 3 consumes it.
# Not committed: it is bulk page content, not source.
body-rescue-*.jsonl

# Index snapshots taken before destructive operations. ~20MB each, every field of every
# record. These are the rollback path, not source — and there was no snapshot of Enhanced
# at all until 2026-08-07, which is why they now exist.
snapshots/

# Generated pilot/run output. One directory per run, each holding results.jsonl and a
# validation pack full of page-text excerpts -- bulk content, regenerable, and it grows one
# directory per experiment.
#
# PATTERN, not instances, and this is the THIRD time that distinction has cost something here:
# the root rules named `docs/60-enrichment/` after the rename (23MB committed), then `cache/`
# and `cache2/` were named literally and `cache-fresh50/` walked past them (636KB committed).
# Structural rule that cannot rot: run output is always a SUBDIRECTORY of reports/, while
# reviewed deliverables (REVIEW-english.md) are FILES at its root.
#
# NOTE for Arijit: `reports/fresh50-run1/` and `fresh50-run2/` are ALREADY TRACKED and this rule
# does not retroactively untrack them -- gitignore does not apply to files already in the index.
# SESSION.md calls the reports "(gitignored)"; that was not true. They are the baseline control
# for the v1.2 comparison, so I have not removed them. Your call, alongside Open item 5.
reports/*/

# Fetched page markdown and the work queue. Bulk page content, regenerable.
# GLOB, not literal names. `cache/` and `cache2/` were listed literally and a third dir,
# `cache-fresh50/`, walked straight past them into a commit -- 636KB of page markdown in a
# PUBLIC repo. Same class as the root rules that pointed at `docs/60-enrichment/` after the
# rename. Name a PATTERN, never an instance.
cache*/
work-queue.jsonl
fetched/

# Rules live HERE, not only in the root .gitignore. The root's enrichment rules pointed at
# `docs/60-enrichment/` for as long as this directory has been called `70-enrichment`, so
# they silently matched nothing and 23MB of payload was committed to a PUBLIC repo against
# the rule's own stated intent. A path-scoped rule in the directory it protects cannot be
# orphaned by renaming that directory.
enhanced-pre-taxonomy-*.jsonl
taxonomy-assignments.jsonl
